# claude
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

#files
sample_forms/*.png
demo/live-preview/*.png
sample_forms/filled/
# frontend/dist/ is COMMITTED, deliberately — see the note in docs/local-setup.md.
# Railway's Railpack builder provisions Python only (the repo root is a Python project),
# so `npm` does not exist in the build image and the frontend cannot be built there.
# Shipping the bundle makes the deploy `pip install` + `uvicorn`, nothing else.
#
# ⚠ THE TRADEOFF: a UI change is not deployed until you rebuild AND commit dist/.
# Forget, and the deploy silently serves the previous bundle.

# packages and venv
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.venv/
supabase/
*.json
# ...but NOT the JSON the build and the form-fill pipeline depend on. Already-tracked
# files are unaffected by a later ignore rule, so this was latent rather than broken —
# a NEW form schema would simply never get committed, and the deploy would 404 the
# review screen with the file sitting happily on the author's disk.
!contracts/schemas/*.json
!package.json
!frontend/package.json
!frontend/package-lock.json
node_modules/

# artifacts and cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.pytest_cache/